==Battleground==
*The enemy base is protected by a [[Base Barrier]] until the boss is defeated.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
*6 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 10.67 seconds<sup>320f</sup>, delay 80~86.67 seconds<sup>2,400f~2,600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Shadow Boxer K]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 53.33~60 seconds<sup>1,600f~1,800f</sup>.
*2 [[Sir Seal]]s spawn, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[One Horn]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 63.33~70 seconds<sup>1,900f~2,100f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Bore Jr.|Bore Jrs]] spawn after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*1 [[R.Ost]] spawns after 113.33 seconds<sup>3,400f</sup>.
*1 [[Commander Ostromeda]] spawns after 186.67 seconds<sup>5,600f</sup>.
*1 [[Poultrio]] spawns as the boss after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
If you don't want to play this stage and confront the nasty threats backing Poultrio, you can cheese it instead. You can use a Talented Li'l Lion Cat with its Shield Piercing Talent to continuously pierce Poultrio's Shield, Soractes's Conjure to break the initial Shield, Bombercat and a Talented iCat to Freeze Poultrio over and over, and Awakened Bahamut to brute force Poultrio. With this lineup, you can easily kill Poultrio and win the stage before R.Ost can even spawn.

This stage takes the idea of the [[Feathergeddon III (Merciless)|third stage]] to its logical conclusion and pairs up Poultrio with some incredibly hard pushing enemies, including an R.Ost, an Ostromeda, and infinite Bore Jrs. While both R.Ost and Ostromeda are time based spawns, R.Ost and Ostromeda appear quickly enough to the point where you will need incredibly strong Uber options to avoid seeing Ostromeda.

While there are infinite Doge Darks and One Horns to work with, as well as 2 Sir Seals spawned at the start of the stage, it is very easy to run out of cash thanks to One Horn having 900,000 health and in general how much cash you need to burn to properly stall Poultrio. This cash problem gets even worse if you are using multiple [[:Category:Mythic Cats|Mythic]]/[[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare]]/[[:Category:Legend Rare Cats|Legend Rare]] Cats since after your second or third expensive unit you will be left with very little cash to work with for the rest of the stage. While you could choose to only send out one big, expensive unit at the start after Poultrio spawns, doing so means that your other expensive units will be on cooldown for a bit longer, which could be the difference between life and death.

No matter whether or not you're using Ubers, for the startoff it is vital you exploit the Doge Darks and Sir Seals for money so you can deploy your heavy units as fast as possible so as to get them off cooldown earlier. Once Poultrio spawns, your main goal at first is trying to get as much damage off it as possible while also killing the Shadow Boxer K, who will tear through your meatshields like butter. Try to use the [[Ototo Corps|Thunderbolt Cannon]] to Freeze the Bore Jr. when he spawns to get [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can]] or something else to snipe him, preventing huge damage from ripping through your units. If that isn't possible, use [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train]] or a lucky [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Doron]] [[Surge Attack]] to get some damage, and from there use an Uber or [[Master of Logic Newtone (Special Cat)|Mewtone]]'s initial hit to clean it up. After R.Ost spawns, the pushing power will rise dramatically, and as such you should try to kill him before Ostromeda spawns, since if you have three R.Ost variants on screen you will lose extremely fast.

Finally, it might be useful to note that this stage is incredibly RNG based. Anything can and will go wrong due to Poultrio's random Explosions and Knockback, which could do everything from preventing [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Uril]] from ever landing a hit to preventing Bullet Train from getting rebounded. Further RNG is also present here from your main meatshields relying on Dodge, as well as Doron's Surge, which could cost you an entire run if it doesn't land on Bore Jr.

===Recommended Units===
*Dodge meatshields: Like in the other three stages, you will need Dodge meatshields to even stand a chance against Poultrio's extremely rapid and powerful attacks. Examples include [[Matador Cat (Rare Cat)|Bellydance Cat]], [[Brainwashed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Mohawk Cat]], [[Talents|Talented]] [[Ninja Cat (Special Cat)|Flying Ninja Cat]], and a Talented [[Bondage Cat (Special Cat)|Ultimate Bondage Cat]]. Because Poultrio and the other enemies will push so quickly, an Uberless clear of this stage will want both Bellydance as well as a second Dodge meatshield to properly stall everyone. From the three options left, you will want to bring Bondage; even though Ninja only requires her Dodge Talent to operate on this stage compared to Bondage demanding both Dodge and the HP Buff Talent, Bondage is much better as a second meatshield alongside Bellydancer due to his much better health.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]]: Boulder is required to bring along on its stage due to its blazing fast speed and recharge and powerful stalling potential, making it extremely helpful to temporarily stall any number of R.Ost variants here. Use Boulder carefully, as if you waste a Boulder by allowing Poultrio to hit both it and a Dodge meatshield, Poultrio can eventually kill the Dodge meatshield then gain immense amounts of ground while your next Boulder is still on its cooldown.
*[[Jetpack Cat (Rare Cat)|Kinjirou Cat]]: Kinjirou is a not terrible meatshield for this stage, being Resistant to Poultrio, Shadow Boxer K, Doge Dark and Ostromeda's traits. Bring Kinjirou with immense caution, however, as his lengthy cooldown makes him immensely risky to bring along as your second line of defense.
*[[Li'l Gau (Rare Cat)|Crystal Li'l Gau Gau]]: Li'l Gau on this stage is like Kinjirou but actually good, having an extremely fast cooldown, Knockback Immune, and great effective health against Poultrio. His low cost also means that you can even use him as a generalist meatshield for when R.Ost or Ostromeda enter the battle.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]]: Jelly is more a desperate pick here than anything else, as Poultrio's Explosions makes Jelly extremely difficult to get valuable damage off with. Nevertheless, you might want Jelly for the Bore Jr. and if Poultrio is properly Slowed/Frozen enough to where Jelly will actually be able to get an attack off before Poultrio speeds into Jelly and blows it up.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]]: Bullet Train maintains its relevance as a quick damaging unit to brute-force Poultrio's [[Shield]] and to deal with the Bore Jr.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: Can Can is best used for the startoff and to deal with the supporting enemies that are not R.Ost variants. Once Poultrio spawns, however, getting Can Can to land hits can be quite the hassle due to Poultrio's large Omni Strike and rapid Explosions. Neverthless, since getting Shadow Boxer K to not hit your Uril is important, you should still try to have Can Can get some sneaky hits in if possible.
*[[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]]: Hitman is a strong [[:Category:Anti-Traitless Cats|anti-Traitless unit]] to specifically deal with R.Ost and the occasional Bore Jr. However, Hitman's low endurance can be quite the issue, and his Long Distance can easily become more of a curse than a blessing if Poultrio has pushed too far.
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] and [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]]: Poultrio pushes crazy hard, meaning that Cyberpunk and Deadeye are welcome additions here alongside your Mythic Cats. However, Cyberpunk's massive blind spot means that even with his Survive Talent, it is incredibly easy for him to become a waste of a slot if Poultrio is able to push even a little bit into your units. While Deadeye's Slow and Knockback is very crippling, you need to make sure there aren't any peons on screen to get Deadeye to not waste his hit.
*[[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Awakened Doron]]: Doron doesn't target any enemy on this stage, but his huge damage and Surge allows him to get some very important cheap damage onto the enemies here, especially Bore Jr. It is vital that Doron's Surge is able to hit Bore Jr., as if it doesn't land you will have a much harder time trying to kill Bore Jr. with haste. It might also be useful to remember that Doron has a crazy amount of health, meaning if you really need to, you can use him as a tank for a few seconds.
*[[Master of Logic Newtone (Special Cat)|Master of Logic Mewtone]]: Mewtone is an extremely powerful super-backliner whose long Slow vs. [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] helps out considerably against both One Horn and the boss itself, and Mewtone's high damage makes him perfect to chip down Shadow Boxer K, Bore Jr., or the other ostriches. His Conjure is also invaluable for pushing back Poultrio or to chip at Bore Jr.
*[[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]]: Uril and his [[True Form]] are practically required for this stage with his powerful [[:Category:Anti-Aku Cats|anti-Aku]] crowd-control, which can disable Poultrio's extremely annoying Knockback. However, Uril is a bit worse here than in the first three stages of this Advent due to the supporting enemies, which can quickly tear through Uril's health.
*Talented [[Filibuster Cat X (Special Cat)|Metafilibuster]]: For Uberless strategies, a Metafilibuster with his Massive Damage and Attack Buff Talents unlocked is the best counter to the R.Ost due to his crushing effective damage against [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] and powerful Freeze, as well as being able to one-shot Bore Jr. However, this doesn't mean he's particularly good, as Metafilibuster's long foreswing is easily interupted by Poultrio's Explosion and Knockbacks, meaning that you need to take particular care when using him.
*[[Giga-Nyan Rex (Uber Rare Cat)|Giga-Nyan Rex]]: Giga-Nyan Rex is really bad most of the time, but given Poultrio's properties Giga-Nyan Rex can actually be useful if you don't have anything else to run. Its short Slow can combo well with Uril and Mewtone, Strong vs. Black, and most importantly Explosion Immunity makes it a decent generalist to use. Think of Giga-Nyan Rex like using [[Miyamoku Musashi (Special Cat)|Heroic Musashi]] on [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 30|Heavenly Tower Floor 30]]: a bad unit with poor stats who has to stand in the back for the boss and slowly chip the enemies down.
*Talented [[Li'l Cow Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Lion Cat]]: For the cheese strategy, Li'l Lion is the best Shield Piercer available to allow your Freeze CC options to stunlock Poultrio due to his fast speed, cooldown, and decently high chance to Pierce Shields. The only Talent you will need on Li'l Lion is to max out his Shield Pierce Talent, as everything else is completely useless.
*[[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] and Talented [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]]: The only reason the cheese even works is because Poultrio lacks immunity to Freeze, being protected only by its regenerating Shield . With Bombercat and an iCat with its Move Speed Up Talent fully maxed out, they can, if given the chance, stunlock Poultrio and stop it from attacking. Even if it flinches, its Shield will be quickly pierced by Li'l Lion before Poultrio recovers. A [[Gardener Cat (Rare Cat)|Weedwacker Cat]] with its Target Aku Talent can also help with consistency, as well as provide a small Initial Money Combo with Bombercat, but you don't need the Target Aku Talent to win. In addition, you should try getting your Bombercat to be at least level 40 to allow it to tank one Poultrio hit.

===Recommended Ubers===
*[[Thundia (Uber Rare Cat)|Ultimate Thundia β]]: Thundia lacks immunities to Poultrio, but her massive nuke damage to Poultrio allows her to ignore those issues. With a multi-hit which can both brute-force the Shield and get a damage knockback onto Poultrio, using Thundia you can get a quick clear of the stage and possibly skip having to fight Ostromeda. As a bonus, her second hit's range can also allow her to work to get huge damage off onto Bore Jr. What puts Thundia over the edge compared to almost every other Uber option for this stage, however, is her being able to abuse Poultrio's Knockbacks to the fullest: often, Thundia will get her first, more damaging hit off on Poultrio, thus either landing a damage knockback or brute-forcing its Shield, then get knocked back by Poultrio, thus allowing her to start her attack again.
*Ultra Talented [[Kai (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Kai μ]]: With her Target Aku and Defense Buff Talents, Kai is able to wall the boss immensely, and her high damage and Shield Piercing Talent can also get a decent chunk out onto the boss. Just make sure she doesn't take much damage from Bore Jr. and the [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark enemies]], as they'll quickly shred through Kai's health.
*[[Sea Serpent Daliasan (Uber Rare Cat)|God-Emperor Daliasan]]: Daliasan has very low endurance, but his high standing range and Knockback Immunity makes him a decent option for Poultrio thanks to his crushing damage and chance at a Savage Blow, which can take out a Bore Jr. if it lands.
*[[Oda Nobunaga (Uber Rare Cat)|Phantasmal Nobunaga]]: A single Phantasmal Nobunaga hit onto an unshielded Poultrio can cripple Poultrio for a huge amount of time, and alongside other DPS options to constantly break Poultrio's Shield you can get a huge amount of damage off before R.Ost spawns. Note that Nobunaga should only be sent out if there aren't too many other enemies on screen, as any kind of support will demonstrate exactly why Nobunaga doesn't have the best reputation among Ubers. Similarly, [[Ice Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Ice Crystal Cat]] also has a lengthy Freeze, although with a shorter foreswing and a shorter Freeze. If you have Ice Cat's Ultra Talents for whatever reason, her Dodge Talent is a considerable help for this stage, and her Strengthen Talent can allow her to dish out a pretty good amount of damage.
*[[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Yukimura]]: Yukimura maintains his relevance as in any other stage, being a rusher to get huge damage off onto Poultrio and then die. Thanks to Poultrio's Knockbacks, if you get lucky you can get a bunch of rebounds and deal huge damage with Yukimura. Also works for the Shadow Boxer K and Bore Jr.
*[[Uesugi Kenshin (Uber Rare Cat)|Hellrider Kenshin]]: Kenshin's good health and double Knockback with her Mini-Wave allows her to push Poultrio to the base as well as chip away at the supporting enemies with said Mini-Wave. Be careful using her, as you can easily get Uril to miss his attack if using her.
*[[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Jizo's Mega-Castle]]: Kasa Jizo's [[Ultra Form]] is really bad for this stage, but his [[True Form]] on the other hand is a decently okay nuker here, albeit with some problems due to his multi-hit potentially creating some problems with Poultrio's Explosions and Knockbacks.
*[[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Supernova Cosmo]]: Admittedly, Cosmo's Ultra Form is not as consistant compared to most other stages in the game, but for a stage as chaotic as this, anything is welcome. Cosmo's crazy range means that given your meatshields don't fail you, Cosmo can get some huge hits which can quickly turn the tide of battle thanks to his high damage and Wave, able to snipe the Bore Jr. and cripple the Shadow Boxer K. You can also use Cosmo's initial hit to first brute-force the Shield, then have the Wave either get a damage knockback or take off large amounts of Poultrio's remaning health.
*[[The White Rabbit (Uber Rare Cat)|The Spectral Cat]]: Spectral Cat's high effective health and damage makes her a really good Uber for Poultrio, as well as having some incredibly powerful CC in the form of a lengthy Slow and crippling Weaken which can easily combo with Uril and Mewtone. As a bonus, her initial hit is able to brute-force Poultrio's Shield, and her second and third hits will then apply the Weaken and Slow onto Poultrio. In particular, she targets both Red and [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]], meaning that she is incredibly good at dealing with the Poultrio and Ostromeda portion of this level.
*Ultra Talented [[Anubis the Protector (Uber Rare Cat)|Almighty Anubis]]: If you have Anubis's Ultra Talents for whatever reason, he is a decently viable option for this stage thanks to his Knockback Immunity, chance of piercing Shields, and high DPS, alongside an unreliable Surge which can nuke a supporting enemy if it actually lands. However, given Poultrio's extremely aggressive nature, the playstyle of luring into Anubis's range to allow his attack to connect is very risky thanks to his long foreswing.
*[[Mighty Drednot (Uber Rare Cat)|B.C.S. Beartooth]]: With its Dodge Talent, B.C.S. Beartooth becomes an incredibly powerful anti-Poultrio nuker able to deal huge amounts of damage onto Poultrio while also having Knockback Immunity and a decent chance to dodge Poultrio's attacks. The Dodge Talent in particular is what makes Beartooth so strong here, being able to withstand a bunch of Poultrio hits while dishing out crazy damage that can remove high amounts of One Horn and the boss's health.
*[[Mighty Bomburr (Uber Rare Cat)|NEK-03 Cloud Emperor]]: Bomburr's Ultra Form isn't the greatest backliner generalist to exist, but even if Untalented, Bomburr's Explosions, if they occur, can force damage knockbacks onto Shadow Boxer K and Bore Jr., and also deal a decent amount of damage onto R.Ost before going down. The main appeal of Bomburr's Ultra Form, though, is its Explosion Immunity, allowing it to stay on the field for a decent amount of time before it finally goes down.
*Ultra Talented [[Sea Maiden Ruri (Uber Rare Cat)|Mer-Queen Ruri]]: With her Dodge Talent, Mer-Queen Ruri acts as a big version of Bellydance, except with actual damage which can get huge damage off on Ostromeda, Shadow Boxer K, and Bore Jr.
*[[Adventurer Kanna (Uber Rare Cat)|Fabled Adventurer Girl Kanna]]: Kanna is another nuker option, but a bit better compared to [[Pai-Pai (Uber Rare Cat)|Pai-Pai]] or [[EVA Unit-02 (Uber Rare Cat)|Eva Unit-02]] due to her Surges and Long Distance, allowing her to chip away at Bore Jr. as well as more importantly deal strong amounts of damage against the Shadow Boxer Ks.
*[[Pai-Pai (Uber Rare Cat)|Pai-Pai DX]]: Pai-Pai's foreswing is really annoying to deal with, but if the Shield has been broken beforehand, she can get a lot of damage onto Poultrio assuming Poultrio has been hit by Uril. Similarly, [[EVA Unit-02 (Uber Rare Cat)|Unit-02, Code 777]] does the same thing as Pai-Pai, being a big nuker for albeit a bit worse due to its Long Distance, foreswing, and lack of effective health against Red.
*[[Child of Destiny Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Destiny Phonoa]]: Phonoa's ridiculous effective DPS and high range allows them to stand safely in the backline as long as your defense is good and chip away at Poultrio and the supporting enemies. To an extent, [[King of Doom Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Extinction Phono]] also does the same job, albeit with a bit more risk as their extremely short Slow can override the Slow of Uril or Mewtone.
*[[Celestial Child Luna (Uber Rare Cat)|Salvation's Daughter Lunacia]]: Lunacia's excellent crowd-control and damage to both the boss and Ostromeda makes her one of the strongest Uber options available for this stage, as well as having Wave Shield for Bore Jr.
*[[Squire Luno (Uber Rare Cat)|Lunos the Luminous]]: Lunos isn't as great against Poultrio's stages compared to most other stages due to its Shield and really strong pushing power, but given that Lunos targets Black, you can use him as a quick tanking option as well as for his Conjure for supporting enemy purposes. Just be careful of your cash, as you can easily go broke if there isn't a One Horn or Doge Dark about to die.
*[[Hajime Saito (Uber Rare Cat)|Hajime Saito]]: Saito's blazing Speed and guaranteed Shield Piercing makes him a pretty good unit here, able to rush into Poultrio to get an extremely damaging hit off.
*[[Baki Hanma (Uber Rare Cat)|Baki Hanma]]: Baki is pretty good here with his high DPS, Explosion Immunity, short cooldown and rapid attacks allowing him to constantly Knockback Poultrio. As a bonus, Baki has a small chance to instantly Pierce Poultrio's Shield.
*[[:Category:Anti-Traitless Cats|Anti-Traitless]] Nukers: R.Ost can easily cripple your run if you use too many specialists for Ostromeda and Poultrio, so you might want to try an anti-Traitless unit to help out. Examples include an Ultra Talented [[Warlock and Pierre (Uber Rare Cat)|Mad Doctor Klay]], [[D'arktanyan (Uber Rare Cat)|Valiant D'arktanyan]], [[Shadow Gao (Uber Rare Cat)|Diabolic Gao]], or [[Izanami of Dusk (Legend Rare Cat)|Izanami of Eventide]].
*[[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|Anti-Alien]] Nukers: If you're not too concerned about R.Ost with your lineup, you may want to consider bringing an Ostromeda counter instead. Examples include Mad Doctor Klay, [[Blanka (Uber Rare Cat)|Blanka]], [[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Almighty Aphrodite]], [[Bazifenix]], or [[Daybreaker Izanagi (Legend Rare Cat)|Dawnbringer Izanagi]].
*Knockback-Immune Ubers: Quite a few Ubers have a Knockback Immunity Talent that often make them worse in almost every scenario possible. However, if you choose to purchase this Talent and thus make your Uber worse for the rest of the game, a lot of Ubers that previously would be deadweights thanks to Poultrio's constant Knockback and Explosion are now able to actually do a decent bit of work here. Examples include [[Mighty Deth-Troy-R (Uber Rare Cat)|Obliterator Diabolosa]], [[Summoner Satoru (Uber Rare Cat)|Devil Hunter Satoru]], [[Hevijak the Wicked (Uber Rare Cat)|God-Emperor Hevijak]], [[Cat Machine (Uber Rare Cat)|Cat Machine Mk 3]], and [[Splendid Ganesha (Uber Rare Cat)|Almighty Ganesha]].
*[[Musashi Miyamoto (Legend Rare Cat)|Immortal Miyamoto]]: You'll often find periods where there are very few enemies on screen, meaning Immortal Miyamoto can easily go to town here with his really high stats against Black. If using Miyamoto, make sure to bring proper counters to R.Ost and Bore Jr., as his damage is lackluster against non-Dark enemies.
*[[Jeanne (Legend Rare Cat)|Divine Jeanne ψ]]: In her True Form, Jeanne gains buffs which allows her to work against Poultrio, although not fully counter it. Jeanne just so happens to stand 10 range away from Poultrio's Omni Strike and be Explosion-Immune, meaning that if you properly protect her she should theoretically be able to work as a really good Explosion-Immune nuker for the boss. However, the fact that she only outranges it by 10 means that you need to run support units like Uril, Mewtone, and have good meatshielding options to prevent her from getting destroyed by Poultrio. In addition, Jeanne has a blind spot, meaning she can miss her attacks if Poultrio just so happens to be unslowed or unfrozen.
*Ultra Talented [[Sharpshooter Saki (Uber Rare Cat)|Bad Blaster Saki]]: If you decide to invest in her Ultra Talents, she can be a solid counter, being immune to Poultrios Explosions. She can also nuke Ostromeda. However, be sure to keep her protected when Bore Jr. and R. Ost appear.
*[[Lone Moon Lunos (Uber Rare Cat)|Lunos the Eclipsed]]: A single conjure is able to kill Doge Darks and Bore Jrs(due to the wave attacks) and gain double money from them, as well as deal considerable damage to the other enemies. Even though he does not target any of Poultrio's traits, he is able to withstand their attacks for a decent time, along with helping to tank R.Ost's and Ostromeda's attacks when Poultrio is slowed/frozen.

